    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classconfig_1_1_theme" kindref="compound">Theme</ref> state model — <computeroutput><ref refid="classconfig_1_1_directory" kindref="compound">config::Directory</ref></computeroutput> subclass that owns the live ValueTree of theme lua files and SVG graphics callbacks. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Manages the full lifecycle for a named theme subdirectory passed as a resolved <computeroutput><ref refid="classjuce_1_1File" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">juce::File</ref>:</computeroutput> </para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classconfig_1_1_theme_1a0c350ee3844fcceaa5d9d68023ae6cdd" kindref="member">initialise()</ref></computeroutput> builds the default tree from <ref refid="namespaceBinaryData" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">BinaryData</ref> (theme.lua, whelmed.lua) so that <computeroutput>saveToPath</computeroutput> can walk it for SVG filenames.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>saveToPath(dir)</computeroutput> writes each theme lua and every graphics SVG listed in the tree into <computeroutput>dir</computeroutput> inline via a local lambda — no shared write method.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>loadFromPath(dir)</computeroutput> clears <computeroutput>state</computeroutput>, reads each lua from disk into the tree, rebuilds <computeroutput>graphicsCallbacks</computeroutput>, then fires <computeroutput>state.sendPropertyChangeMessage(ID::theme)</computeroutput> last.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>fileChanged(...)</computeroutput> on <computeroutput>fileUpdated</computeroutput> for <computeroutput></computeroutput>.lua — calls <computeroutput>loadFromPath</computeroutput> (which handles the notify); for <computeroutput></computeroutput>.svg — dispatches via <computeroutput>graphicsCallbacks</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>LookAndFeel listens on the <computeroutput>ID::theme</computeroutput> notify channel.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classconfig_1_1_directory" kindref="compound">config::Directory</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classend_1_1_look_and_feel" kindref="compound">end::LookAndFeel</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
